 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The sky is on her; she glides along,\nShe leads a swan in the water's tide;\nAnd she speaks, and sings to the ocean\nWith the song of the ocean.\nThe waters blow their voices\nInto the depths where the waves occur,\nWhere winds are low and breezes,\nWhen the clouds of thunder\nDrown all the waters over over.\nAnd she sees my heart with others\nFain would rejoice when alone;\nYet I know that alone",
